9,0,7,7,0,9,0,7,7],[7,0,7,0,7,7,0,7,0,7,0,9,0,7,7,0,9,0,7,7],[7,0,0,0,7,7,0,0,0,7,0,0,0,7,7,0,0,0,7,7]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"**What the grid is made of.** Every structure built from 0s is a \"pipe\". It has two parts:\n- a 3×3 **head**: two full sides plus a back wall, open on one side;\n- a 1-cell-wide **shaft** that runs from the head's back wall across the grid.\n\nThe open side of the head holds some contents: 9s or plain 7s.\n\n**What changes.**\n- **Pair 1:** each head sits at the left (x=0..2) with its shaft running right to x=13. In the output, the shaft is gone and the same 3×3 head, with the same orientation and contents (`9 7 0` or `7 7 0`), sits at the far end of the shaft (x=11..13).\n- **Pair 3:** the mirror case. Heads at the right edge slide to x=0..2, carrying their contents (`0 7 9`, `0 9 9`, `0 7 7`).\n- **Pair 2:** the same thing vertically. The heads at rows 5..7 move to rows 0..2, and the contents (7, 9) come along.\n\n9s that are not inside a head (for example the `9 9` at row 6 of pair 1, or the 9 at (7,4) in pair 2) stay where they are.\n\n**The rule.** For each pipe:\n1. Copy the 3×3 head box, including its contents.\n2. Erase the head box and the whole shaft to background.\n3. Paste the head unchanged at the opposite end of the shaft, so its outer edge lands where the shaft ended.\n\n**Finding the head in code.**\n- A pipe whose bounding box is 3 rows tall is horizontal. Its head columns are the columns where the top row of the box is 0.\n- A vertical pipe is handled by transposing the grid first.\n- The head moves to whichever end of the bounding box it is not already at.\n\n**Test input.** There are four vertical pipes with heads at rows 0..2, holding various 9/7 contents. Their shafts run down to row 19, so each head moves to rows 17..19. All the 9s in the test sit inside head boxes, so they all travel with their heads.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    comps = components(g == 0)\n    for cells in comps:\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = bbox(cells)\n        vertical = (y1 - y0 + 1) != 3\n        src = g.T if vertical else g\n        dst = out.T if vertical else out   # views, edits propagate\n        if vertical:\n            y0, x0, y1, x1 = x0, y0, x1, y1\n        hcols = [x for x in range(x0, x1 + 1) if src[y0, x] == 0]\n        hx0, hx1 = min(hcols), max(hcols)\n        head = src[y0:y0 + 3, hx0:hx1 + 1].copy()\n        w = hx1 - hx0 + 1\n        nx0 = x1 - w + 1 if hx0 == x0 else x0\n        # erase shaft and head\n        for (cy, cx) in cells:\n            out[cy, cx] = bg\n        dst[y0:y0 + 3, hx0:hx1 + 1] = bg\n        dst[y0:y0 + 3, nx0:nx0 + w] = head\n        emit(out, \"Removed a pipe's shaft and slid its 3x3 head, with contents, to the far end of the shaft.\")\n    emit(out, \"All pipe heads moved to the opposite ends of their shafts.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"rigid":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- **Pair 3:** the mirror case."}],"movement":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Heads at the right edge slide to x=0..2, carrying their contents (`0 7 9`, `0 9 9`, `0 7 7`)."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- A pipe whose bounding box is 3 rows tall is horizontal."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- The head moves to whichever end of the bounding box it is not already at."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"62520e4641902127ea189fc1880348bce90ff6d8dfb4002571449c0b66666919","task_sha256":"607d0eb0397673fa13b60d410f28467d036e618ebb84bd0d283ce8142b82989f","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
